    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image19-231c555a-6449-40d5-8760-08aa65321a94.jpg\" style=\"height: 141px; width: 200px;\" /><br /><br />As we are are moving away from <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> toward sheet <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> spacing between electric lines of force is increasing. <math><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></math> In direction of electric field potential decreases. <math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow></msub><mtext> </mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi></mrow></msub></math>",
